"text": "For this California job, the oxygen range to test for is 19.5 to 23.5 percent. \nThe confined space limits are the same in both systems: oxygen 19.5 to 23.5 percent and 10 percent of the LEL.\n\n- Federal side: \noxygen below 19.5 percent is deficient and above 23.5 percent is enriched (fire hazard)\n. In California the same duties sit in Title 8 sections 1950 to 1962.\n- Meters for sewer entry should sound an audible alarm at \nOxygen concentration less than 19.5 percent\n.\n- Oxygen is only one test. \nThese numbers describe a hazardous atmosphere; they do not by themselves make a space safe to enter.\n Also test LEL, H2S and CO.\n\nYour competent person or entry supervisor decides on site whether entry can proceed.",
